        {
          "id": "e40671d1-8591-4ab1-af90-412bebc89339",
          "memory": "Jen's cute polka-dot umbrella broke on her morning walk to work on September 25, 2026 when a gust flipped it inside out and snapped a spoke after about two years of use; her left shoulder was drenched, shoes were squeaking, and she planned to trash it and buy a cheap replacement at the drugstore across the street at lunch.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "0d044749-7944-4b90-bfda-a0df9d794eac",
          "memory": "On the morning of September 25, 2026 User could not sleep after User's cat woke User around 6am by sitting on User's pillow staring at User then demanding breakfast immediately, and User was already on a second cup of coffee at User's desk by morning.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "d0d755a5-a6a5-45ae-a508-60be9665afa8",
          "memory": "User's package finally arrived on September 24, 2026 with the box all dented but the contents inside were fine, as User told Jen on September 25, 2026.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "85b027b5-db46-4ed8-857c-151f30953f80",
          "memory": "On September 25, 2026 Jen said facilities reported her office lobby was leaking again with buckets out by the elevators, and User warned her to be careful walking there with wet shoes so she would not wipe out.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "b1ccecd3-ccb0-4709-bc52-af93c15effba",
          "memory": "On the morning of September 25, 2026 Jen had about 40 unread emails mostly cc nonsense and said she could not archive them because her boss checks, while User said User archives half without reading; Jen had a backup sweater in her office drawer and was in line for a big coffee.",
          "event": "ADD"
        }
      ]
    },
